enters\nProjects\nInstitutes\nOutreach\nResources\nHappenings\nNews\nEvents\nPublications\nSocial Media\nPress Releases\nFriends & Giving\nGIVE TO SEHD\nAlumni & Volunteers\nCommunity Partners\nAbout Us\nPrograms\nAdmission\nPeople\nStudents\nOur Work\nHappenings\nFriends & Giving\nToggle navigation\nSEHD Home\nSEHD Home\nSEHD News\nDepartment of Educational and Psychological Studies\nDepartment of Kinesiology and Sport Sciences\nDepartment of Teaching and Learning\nSearch\nSearch\nApplication Deadlines\nDoctoral Application Process\nMasters Application Process\nInternational Application Process\nFrequently Asked Questions\nOrientation\nStaff\nAbout Us\nMeet the Dean\nHistory\nMission\nAccreditation\nPrograms\nMaster's Programs\nDoctoral Programs\nBachelor's Programs\nOnline Programs\nCertificate Programs\nMinors\nPrograms by Department\nAdmission\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nFinancial Aid\nTuition\nContact Us\nPeople\nAdministration\nFaculty\nStaff\nEmeritus Faculty\nStudents\nScholarships\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nInternational Students\nOrganizations\nJob & Internship Openings\nWell-Being\nOur Work\nResearch\nCenters\nProjects\nInstitutes\nOutreach\nResources\nHappenings\nNews\nEvents\nPublications\nSocial Media\nPress Releases\nFriends & Giving\nGIVE TO SEHD\nAlumni & Volunteers\nCommunity Partners\nSEHD Home\nSEHD Home\nSEHD News\nDepartment of Educational and Psychological Studies\nDepartment of Kinesiology and Sport Sciences\nDepartment of Teaching and Learning\nApplication Deadlines\nDoctoral Application Process\nMasters Application Process\nInternational Application Process\nFrequently Asked Questions\nOrientation\nStaff\nAbout Us\nListening Exercise\nPrograms\nCommunications\nHistory\nContact Us\nHome\nAdmission\nGraduate\nDoctoral Application Process\nAAA\nDoctoral Application Process\nApplication Deadlines\nDoctoral Application Process\nMasters Application Process\nInternational Application Process\nFrequently Asked Questions\nOrientation\nStaff\nGET STARTED\n1\nRequest Info\n2\nVisit\n3\nApply\nStep 1: Sign Up for a Graduate School Application Account\nVisit the Graduate School Application website to create your account. Please note that your application is not complete, and we cannot begin reviewing it until all required forms are submitted. The $85 non-refundable application fee can be paid online when you submit your Graduate School Application.\nStep 2: Send Official Transcripts\nA Master's degree in an appropriate field, may be required. The degree must be in addition to a bachelor's degree. All degrees must be from regional accredited institutions.\nRequest one official transcript from each post-secondary institution (college or university) that you have attended. Transcripts should be for both undergraduate and graduate.\nApplicants should request transcripts to be sent directly from the institution to us electronically via sehdgradadmissions@miami.edu or to our physical address if electronic transfer is not an option:\nOffice of Graduate Studies\n1507 Levante Ave.\nSuite 311\nCoral Gables, Florida\nStep 3: Letters of Recommendation\nIn your Graduate School Application, in the \"references\" section, you can add you recommender's names and email addresses. When you submit your application they will receive by email a recommendation form to respond and will be able to add a letter on their letterhead. They will then click to send which will come to me electronically.\nStep 4: Send Official GRE Scores\nRequest your GRE general, and TOEFL (if applicable) scores from ETS (University of Miami Institution Code # 5815). ** Transcripts and test scores are not considered as official if provided by, or received via the applicant.\nStep 5: Complete the Essay\nStudents should attach to the application a statement of academic and professional goals. The statement has a maximum length of 2 pages double spaced.\nStep 6: Send CV or Resume\nStudents should attach to the application a current curriculum vitae (CV) or resume.\nStep 7: For International Students Only\nInternational students are required to submit the following items:\nTOEFL (if applicable) scores from ETS (University of Miami Institution Code # 5815). Transcripts and test scores are NOT considered as official if provided by, or received via the applicant.\nEnglish Language Test\nMinimum Score*\nTOEFL (iBT)\n80 (before January 21, 2026)\n4.5 (after January 21, 2026)\nIELTS (Academic)\n6.5\nDuolingo English Test\n125\nA copy of passport.\nCopy of diploma with English translation for degrees earned outside of the United States.\nOfficial / original transcripts with English translation.\nFor more informations click here.\nContact\nGraduate Admissions Office\nMax Orovitz Building\n1507 Levante Avenue \u2013 Suite 311\nCoral Gables Florida 33146\n305.284.2167 phone\n305 284-9395 fax\nsehdgradadmissions@miami.edu\nTop\nUniversity of Miami\nCoral Gables, FL 33124\n305-284-2211\nSchool of Education and Human Development\n5202 University Drive\nMerrick Bldg. Rm. 312\nCoral Gables,\nFL\n33124\n305-284-3711\n305-284-3711\nResources\nAbout UM\nmyUM\nCaneLink\nAcademic Calendar\nCanvas/Blackboard\nUM Network\nAlumni & Friends\nMedical Center\nHurricane Sports\nCareers\nVisit\nCampus Map\nParking & Transportation\nConnect\nsocial-facebook\nsocial-twitter\nsocial-youtube\nsocial-instagram\nCopyright: 2026 University of Miami. All Rights Reserved.\nEmergency Information\nPrivacy Statement & Legal Notices\nIndividuals with disabilities who experience any technology-based barriers accessing University websites can submit details to our online form.", "links": [["Skip to Content", "https://www.edu.miami.edu/admission/graduate/doctoral-app-process/index.html#accessibility-content"], ["Skip to Search", "https://www.edu.miami.edu/admission/graduate/doctoral-app-process/index.html#default-js-input"], ["Skip to footer", "https://www.edu.miami.edu/admission/graduate/doctoral-app-process/index.html#global_footer"], ["Office of Disability Services", "